# Generated native folders — ANCHORED TO THE PROJECT ROOT, AND THEY MUST STAY
# ANCHORED.
#
# .easignore follows gitignore matching: a pattern with no leading slash matches
# a directory of that name at ANY depth. Adding a bare `ios/` here on 5 Sep 2026
# therefore excluded modules/pawtchi-live-activity/ios as well — the local Expo
# module's whole native implementation (podspec + Swift) — while leaving its
# expo-module.config.json and index.ts in place.
#
# Nothing failed. The module simply did not autolink, requireOptionalNativeModule
# returned null, and the walk Live Activity stopped appearing on the Lock Screen
# in every build made after that commit. A native feature disappearing from a
# GREEN build is the expensive kind of mistake, which is why the leading slash
# below is load-bearing rather than cosmetic.
#
# `/ios` and `/android` are the prebuild output at the project root, regenerated
# on the EAS worker. Any native source that lives OUTSIDE them has to be
# uploaded. See lib/build/easignore.test.ts.
/ios
/android
email-preview.html
.tmp-assets/
